  looks like lee was indeed just hyping up  the company but amex would eventually  answer these urban legends by launching  the card for real  [Music]  now that the mx black is actually a real  thing it comes with a slew of defined  benefits starting with elite status at  hospitality brands the card comes with  isg platinum elite hilton honors diamond  marriott bon voy gold and roules and  chateau 5c  in terms of travel you get delta  skymal's platinum medallion status which  includes priority waitlisting priority  checking and boarding it and courtesy  upgrades if you have this card though  waiting at the airport probably wouldn't  be that bad anyways because you get  access to the global lounge collection  this includes lounges that are branded  centuriana mx priority pass escape delta  sky club plaza premium and aerospace you  also get an invitation to hertz's  platinum status and avis presidents club  aside from travel benefits you get a  bunch of retail benefits as well for  example you get to be a part of the  centurion shopping program and you also  get one of the fx membership points on  purchases over five thousand dollars but  honestly none of these perks are really  that special the mx platinum card has  most of the same perks and has better  rewards as well for example the amex  platinum offers 5x membership points on  flights and prepaid hotels now it's not  like the amex platinum is cheap given  that it costs 695 dollars per year but  it's just a fraction of the cost of the  mx black and it comes with all of the  same tangible benefits so if you're just  looking to turn credit cards and earn  rewards there's absolutely no reason to  get the black the only reason to get the  black is if you're looking for vip  service and this is where the black  really shines and i think the best way  to really understand the caliber of  their vip service is by simply looking  at stories take chinese billionaire lou  you can for example  lou is an avid art collector and often  buys paintings that are worth tens of  millions if not over a hundred million  but instead of writing a check or  completing a wire transfer to buy these  paintings lu likes to put it on his amex  card one time he put a 36 million tea  cup from the ming dynasty onto his amex  but by far his most outrageous credit  card purchase was a 170 million dollar  painting this purchase alone would have  earned him a 170 million mx membership  points depending on how he redeemed  these points he could get 1.7 million to  3.4 million worth of rewards thanks to  his purchase not to mention it amex  allowed him to bypass chinese transfer  laws you see china does not allow its  citizens to transfer more than fifty  thousand dollars out of their country in  any given year but since lou charged it  on a credit card he definitely wasn't  transferring any money out of china he  was just paying off his credit card i  suspect that the ccp wasn't that happy  to hear about this purchase aside from  approving crazy large purchases amex  also bends to basically any customer  desire as long as it's not illegal of  course you could say they live by the  motto we shall never deny a guest even  the most ridiculous request and believe  me they get some ridiculous requests for  example this one amex black client was  staying on a private island when they  ran out of ice cubes instead of getting  more eyes from their beach house or just  drinking the rest of their drink without  ice the client decided to call amex and  ask for ice and sure enough amex ended  up playing out a bag of ice declined on  a helicopter this other client asked  amex to deliver flowers to eight  girlfriends in four different states and  three different countries and mx of  course ended up doing it while there are  some crazy stories of people abusing the  system like this the vast majority of  centurion customers don't actually make  such requests more times than not they  just want their entire travel experience  